  "allowLong": false,
  "script": "YouTube just moved your Subscriptions button, and some people are not happy about where it went.\n\nFor nearly a decade it sat in the bottom bar. YouTube confirmed this week that, on Android and iPhone, it's leaving. It's renamed Subs, and it lives in the top bar on the Home tab, right after Home.\n\nWhy would a button move upset anyone? YouTube tested this in May, and people pushed back. That bottom button was how a lot of them skipped the algorithm: one tap showed only the channels they chose. Now it's a reach up top, one tab over from the recommendations.\n\nThe top bar gets busier, too. Live and Music get their own feeds. Movies and TV shows up only if you pay for something like a Primetime Channel.\n\nThere's also a new plus sign up there. Type a topic or a mood, like guided meditations under ten minutes, and YouTube builds a feed around it. Free accounts can save three. Premium members get eight.\n\nThose custom feeds start in the US, in English. YouTube hasn't given a date for the new layout anywhere else.\n\nSo, once your thumb relearns it: will you still check Subs first, or just stay on Home?",
